From bf1eeee129ad76d5a6c250579a198aee78ede693 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 20:36:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] pilotd: direct mode, the owner's Groq and Jev keys on the
 phone

[direct] enabled = true with $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/shoal-pilot/keys.env
present (PILOT_RELAY_GROQ_KEY, PILOT_RELAY_JEV_KEY; refused unless
0600) sends the standard backend straight to the relay's upstreams,
Groq's chat completions and Jev's systemone, each with its own bearer
key and no token exchange. Requests are shaped as the relay's policy.rs
shapes them (Jev state cut down, completion cap 4096, no store, metadata,
user or streaming) and Groq's tool_use_failed 400 becomes the relay's
422. The reply is stamped with the configured region (us for Groq's
public endpoint), replacing anything the upstream says, so the
fail-closed region check stays. Web search needs the relay and is not
offered. A missing key file means the relay as before.

pilotd also reads /etc/shoal-pilot/pilotd.toml when the person has no
config of their own.
